{"id":"SEC-002","category":"architecture","criterion":"resilience","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/evals/harness/run-ablation.sh","line":806,"code_snippet":"required = int(math.ceil(now + 2 * sum(float(e.get(\"watchdog_s\") or 0) for e in plan) / max(conc, 1)))","reasoning_trace":"watchdog_s is already 2 x the phase sum (RAB-1: a1 build phase_sum 140 min, watchdog 16800 s). The sum runs over every plan entry: a0_bare trials (which uses_codex() excludes from codex_arms at 793-794 but not from the sum) and, on --resume, every already-rowed trial (header 116). RAB-30's own comment pins the defect: required_until = now + 2 x (9600 + 16800) / 3 while codex_arms is [\"a1_full\"]. Two arms x twelve build tasks x three trials at concurrency 3 gives 950,400 x 2 / 3 s = 7.3 days against a token lifetime the commit trail records as about ten days (DEC-0593, valid to 2026-10-28); the full suite is refused at any concurrency.","finding":"The codex horizon over-counts by about 4x and includes non-codex arms and finished trials, so large batches, dry-run pre-registrations and late resumes are refused with a remedy (re-login) that cannot satisfy the horizon","critique":"Fail-closed, so no data is harmed, but the runner cannot run the batches the suite defines.","remediation":"Sum only trials that will launch (not in the done set on --resume) for arms where uses_codex is true; use the phase sum or one watchdog, not 2 x watchdog; optionally WARN above the token lifetime instead of refusing. Add RAB cases: a0-heavy plan passes when only the a1 share fits; a --resume with one trial left needs one trial's horizon. Update header 110-119.","confidence":"medium","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/682.html"]}
